hadiths[81]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Ismail, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, informed us, from Qays, he said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, stood and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, you recite this verse: O you who believe, upon you are yourselves; he who strays will not harm you if you are guided, and we heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If people see evil and do not denounce it, Allah will soon envelop them all in His punishment."
"2","Waki narrated to us, he said: Misar and Sufyan narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughira al-Thaqafi, from Ali ibn Rabia al-Walibi, from Asma ibn al-Hakam al-Fazari, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Whenever I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah benefited me with whatever of it He willed, and when anyone else narrated to me from him I made him swear an oath, and if he swore to me I believed him; and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, and Abu Bakr spoke the truth, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no man who commits a sin and then performs ablution and performs ablution well, Misar said: and prays, and Sufyan said: then prays two rakas, and seeks forgiveness from Allah, mighty and majestic, except that He forgives him."
"3","Amr ibn Muhammad Abu Said, meaning al-Anqazi, narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: Abu Bakr bought a saddle from Azib for thirteen dirhams. He said: Abu Bakr said to Azib: Tell al-Bara to carry it to my house. He said: No, until you narrate to us how you acted when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out while you were with him. He said: Abu Bakr said: We set out and traveled by night and hastened our day and night until midday appeared and the midday heat stood, and I looked to see whether I could see any shade to shelter in, and I saw a rock, so I went toward it, and some of its shade remained, so I smoothed it for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and spread a fur for him and said: Lie down, O Messenger of Allah, so he lay down. Then I went out to look to see whether I could see anyone of the pursuers, and I saw a shepherd of sheep, and I said: To whom do you belong, boy? He said: To a man of Quraysh, and he named him, and I recognized him. I said: Is there any milk in your sheep? He said: Yes. I said: Will you milk for me? He said: Yes. So I ordered him and he tied a sheep from among them, then I ordered him and he shook the dust from its udder, then I ordered him and he shook the dust from his hands, and with me was a water-skin with a cloth on its mouth, so he milked for me a measure of milk, and I poured water upon the cup until its bottom cooled. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found him awake, and I said: Drink, O Messenger of Allah, so he drank until I was satisfied. Then I said: Has the time of departure come? He said: So we departed while the people were seeking us, and none of them reached us except Suraqa ibn Malik ibn Jushum on his horse. I said: O Messenger of Allah, this pursuer has caught up with us. He said: Do not grieve, Allah is with us. Until when he drew near us, with a spear-length or two or three between us, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, this pursuer has caught up with us, and I wept. He said: Why do you weep? He said: I said: By Allah, I do not weep for myself, but I weep for you. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated against him and said: O Allah, suffice us against him however You will. So the legs of his horse sank to its belly in hard ground, and he leapt from it and said: O Muhammad, I know this is your doing, so supplicate Allah to deliver me from what I am in, and by Allah I will blind those behind me among the pursuers from you, and this is my quiver, so take an arrow from it, for you will pass by my camels and sheep in such-and-such place, so take from them what you need. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have no need of them. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for him, so he was released, and he returned to his companions, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on with me until we arrived at Medina. The people met him and came out in the road and on the rooftops, and the servants and boys hastened in the road saying: Allah is Most Great, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has come, Muhammad has come. He said: And the people disputed as to which of them he would stay with. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will stay tonight with the Banu al-Najjar, the maternal uncles of Abd al-Muttalib, to honor them thereby. When morning came he went where he was commanded. Al-Bara ibn Azib said: The first of the emigrants who came to us was Musab ibn Umayr, brother of Banu Abd al-Dar, then Ibn Umm Maktum the blind, brother of Banu Fihr, came to us, then Umar ibn al-Khattab came to us with twenty riders. We said: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do? He said: He is following me. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with Abu Bakr with him. Al-Bara said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not arrive until I had memorized suras of the Mufassal. Israil said: Al-Bara was of the Ansar, of Banu Haritha."
"4","Waki narrated to us, he said: Israil said: Abu Ishaq said, from Zayd ibn Yuthay, from Abu Bakr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him with Baraa to the people of Mecca: No polytheist shall perform pilgrimage after this year, and no naked person shall circumambulate the House, and none shall enter Paradise except a Muslim soul; whoever had a treaty between him and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his term is until his term, and Allah is disassociated from the polytheists, and His Messenger. He said: So he traveled with it three days, then he said to Ali, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him: Catch up with him, return Abu Bakr to me, and convey it yourself. He said: So he did. He said: When Abu Bakr came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he wept and said: O Messenger of Allah, has something happened concerning me? He said: Nothing has happened concerning you except good, but I was commanded that none convey it except me or a man from me."
"5","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, from Sulaym ibn Amir, from Awsat, he said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in this place of mine last year, and Abu Bakr wept. Abu Bakr said: Ask Allah for well-being, or he said: health, for no one was ever given after certainty anything better than health, or well-being. Hold to truthfulness, for it is with righteousness, and both are in Paradise. Beware of lying, for it is with wickedness, and both are in the Fire. Do not envy one another, do not hate one another, do not sever ties, do not turn your backs on one another, and be brothers as Allah Almighty commanded you."
"6","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abu Amir narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Abdullah, meaning Ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muadh ibn Rifaa ibn Rafi al-Ansari, from his father Rifaa ibn Rafi, he said: I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, say upon the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, and Abu Bakr wept when he mentioned the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he recovered, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say in this intense heat last year: Ask Allah for pardon and well-being and certainty in the Hereafter and in this world."
"7","Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Atiq, from his father, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The tooth-stick purifies the mouth and pleases the Lord."
"8","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, that he said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Teach me a supplication to supplicate with in my prayer. He said: Say: O Allah, I have wronged myself with much wrongdoing, and none forgives sins except You, so forgive me with forgiveness from You and have mercy on me; You are the Forgiving, the Merciful. And Yunus said: great. Hasan al-Ashyab narrated it to us from Ibn Lahia, he said: he said: great."
"9","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that Fatima and al-Abbas came to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, seeking their inheritance from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then seeking his land of Fadak and his share of Khaybar. Abu Bakr said to them: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: We are not inherited; what we leave is charity; the family of Muhammad only eats from this wealth. By Allah, I will not abandon any matter I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do therein except that I do it."
"10","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Haywa ibn Shurayh narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn al-Harith say that Abu Hurayra said: I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, upon this minbar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on this day last year, then Abu Bakr sobbed and wept, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: You have not been given anything after the word of sincerity like well-being, so ask Allah for well-being."
"11","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us, from Anas, that Abu Bakr narrated to him, he said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the cave, and once he said: while we were in the cave: If one of them looked at his feet he would see us beneath his feet. He said: So he said: O Abu Bakr, what do you think of two with whom Allah is the third."
"12","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from al-Mughira ibn Subay, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us that the Dajjal will emerge from a land in the east called Khurasan, followed by peoples whose faces are like hammered shields."
"13","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said: Sadaqa ibn Musa, the flour merchant, narrated to us, from Farqad, from Murra ibn Sharahil, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No miser shall enter Paradise, nor deceitful person, nor traitor, nor one evil in mastery, and the first to knock at the gate of Paradise are the slaves, when they do well between themselves and Allah, mighty and majestic, and between themselves and their masters."
"14","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us; Abdullah said: And I heard it from Abdullah ibn Abi Shayba, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Jumay, from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken, Fatima sent to Abu Bakr: Did you inherit the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or his family? He said: So he said: No, rather his family. She said: Then where is the share of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Abu Bakr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah, mighty and majestic, feeds a prophet sustenance and then takes him, He makes it for the one who stands after him; so I judged to return it to the Muslims. She said: Then you, and what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), know best."
"15","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Talaqani narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl al-Mazini narrated to me, he said: Abu Naama narrated to me, he said: Abu Hunayda al-Bara ibn Nawfal narrated to me, from Walan al-Adawi, from Hudhayfa, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose one morning and prayed the dawn prayer, then sat until, when it was mid-morning, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, then sat in his place until he prayed the noon, afternoon, and sunset prayers, each time not speaking, until he prayed the last evening prayer, then stood to his family. The people said to Abu Bakr: Will you not ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what is the matter with him; today he did something he never did. He said: So he asked him, and he said: Yes, there was displayed to me what will be of the affair of this world and the affair of the Hereafter; the first and the last were gathered on one plain, and the people were terrified thereby until they went to Adam, peace be upon him, with sweat almost bridling them, and said: O Adam, you are the father of mankind, and Allah, mighty and majestic, chose you; intercede for us with your Lord. He said: I have met the like of what you met; go to your father after your father, to Nuh: Allah chose Adam and Nuh and the family of Ibrahim and the family of Imran above the worlds. He said: So they go to Nuh, peace be upon him, and say: Intercede for us with your Lord, for Allah chose you and answered you in your supplication, and left not a single disbeliever upon the earth. He says: That is not with me; go to Ibrahim, peace be upon him, for Allah, mighty and majestic, took him as a close friend. So they go to Ibrahim, and he says: That is not with me, but go to Musa, peace be upon him, for Allah, mighty and majestic, spoke to him directly. Musa, peace be upon him, says: That is not with me, but go to Isa son of Maryam, for he healed the blind and the leper and gave life to the dead. Isa says: That is not with me, but go to the master of the children of Adam, for he is the first for whom the earth will split on the Day of Resurrection; go to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and let him intercede for you with your Lord, mighty and majestic. He said: So he sets out, and Jibril, peace be upon him, comes to his Lord, and Allah, mighty and majestic, says: Permit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. He said: So Jibril sets out with him, and he falls prostrate for the measure of a week, and Allah, mighty and majestic, says: Raise your head, O Muhammad, and speak and you will be heard, and intercede and you will be granted intercession. He said: So he raises his head, and when he looks at his Lord, mighty and majestic, he falls prostrate for the measure of another week. Allah, mighty and majestic, says: Raise your head and speak and you will be heard, and intercede and you will be granted intercession. He said: So he goes to fall prostrate, and Jibril, peace be upon him, takes him by his upper arms, and Allah, mighty and majestic, opens for him supplications He never opened for any human before, and he says: My Lord, You created me the master of the children of Adam, and no boast, and the first for whom the earth will split on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast, until there comes to me at the Basin more than between Sana and Ayla. Then it is said: Call the truthful, and they intercede. Then it is said: Call the prophets. He said: So a prophet comes with a company, and a prophet with five or six, and a prophet with none with him. Then it is said: Call the martyrs, and they intercede for whomever they wish. He said: When the martyrs do that, he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: I am the Most Merciful of the merciful; admit to My Paradise whoever did not associate anything with Me. He said: So they enter Paradise. He said: Then Allah, mighty and majestic, says: Look into the Fire, do you find anyone who ever did any good? He said: So they find a man in the Fire, and it is said to him: Did you ever do any good? He says: No, except that I was lenient with people in buying and selling. Allah, mighty and majestic, says: Be lenient with My servant as he was lenient with My servants. Then they bring out of the Fire a man, and it is said to him: Did you ever do any good? He says: No, except that I commanded my children: when I die, burn me with fire, then grind me until, when I am like kohl, take me to the sea and scatter me in the wind, for by Allah the Lord of the worlds will never be able to seize me. Allah, mighty and majestic, says: Why did you do that? He says: Out of fear of You. Allah, mighty and majestic, says: Look at the dominion of the greatest king, for you shall have its like and ten times its like. He says: Why do You mock me while You are the King? He said: And that is what I laughed at in the mid-morning."
"16","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muawiya, narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, stood and praised Allah, mighty and majestic, and extolled Him, and said: O people, you recite this verse: O you who believe, upon you are yourselves; he who strays will not harm you if you are guided, to the end of the verse, and you place it in other than its place, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If people see evil and do not change it, Allah will soon envelop them in His punishment. He said: And I heard Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, say: O people, beware of lying, for lying is apart from faith."
"17","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Khumayr informed me, he said: I heard Sulaym ibn Amir, a man of Himyar, narrating from Awsat ibn Ismail ibn Awsat al-Bajali, narrating from Abu Bakr, that he heard him when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in this place of mine last year, then wept, then said: Hold to truthfulness, for it is with righteousness, and both are in Paradise, and beware of lying, for it is with wickedness, and both are in the Fire. Ask Allah for well-being, for no man was given after certainty anything better than well-being. Then he said: Do not sever ties, do not turn your backs on one another, do not hate one another, do not envy one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers."
"18","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abdullah al-Awdi, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while Abu Bakr was in a district of Medina. He said: So he came and uncovered his face and kissed him and said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, how sweet you are alive and dead; Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has died, by the Lord of the Kaba. Then he mentioned the hadith. He said: So Abu Bakr and Umar set out walking together until they came to them. Abu Bakr spoke and left nothing revealed concerning the Ansar, nor mentioned by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of their affair, except that he mentioned it, and said: You know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people take a valley and the Ansar take a valley, I would take the valley of the Ansar. And you know, O Sad, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, while you were sitting: Quraysh are the rulers of this affair; the righteous of the people follow their righteous, and their wicked follow their wicked. He said: Sad said to him: You spoke the truth; we are the ministers and you are the commanders."
"19","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: al-Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: A man of Basra narrated to me, from Talha ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: I heard my father mention that his father heard Abu Bakr say: I said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, is action upon what has already been concluded, or upon a matter newly begun? He said: Rather upon a matter already concluded. He said: I said: Then wherein is action, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Each is facilitated for what he was created for."
"20","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: A man of the Ansar, of the people of understanding, informed me that he heard Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah have mercy on him, narrate: That men of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, grieved for him until some of them almost fell into delusion; Uthman said: And I was among them. While I was sitting in the shade of a fortress of the fortresses, Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, passed by me and greeted me, and I did not perceive that he passed or greeted. Umar went until he entered upon Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and said to him: What pleases you is that I passed by Uthman and greeted him, and he did not return the greeting? He and Abu Bakr came, in the caliphate of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, until they both greeted me together. Then Abu Bakr said: Your brother Umar came to me and mentioned that he passed by you and greeted, and you did not return the greeting; what carried you to that? He said: I said: I did not do it. Umar said: Indeed, by Allah you did, but it is your arrogance, O Banu Umayya. He said: I said: By Allah I did not perceive that you passed by me, nor greeted. Abu Bakr said: Uthman spoke the truth, and were you preoccupied from that by a matter? I said: Yes. He said: What is it? Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Allah, mighty and majestic, took His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before we asked him about the salvation of this affair. Abu Bakr said: I asked him about that. He said: So I stood to him and said to him: May my father and mother be ransom for you, you are most entitled to it. Abu Bakr said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the salvation of this affair? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever accepts from me the word I offered to my uncle, and he rejected it from me, it is salvation for him."
"21","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbih narrated to us, he said: Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: A shaykh of Quraysh narrated to me, from Raja ibn Haywa, from Junada ibn Abi Umayya, from Yazid ibn Abi Sufyan, he said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said when he sent me to Sham: O Yazid, you have kinship; perhaps you will favor them with command, and that is what I fear most for you, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is put in charge of any affair of the Muslims and appoints over them anyone out of favoritism, upon him is the curse of Allah; Allah accepts from him neither exchange nor compensation until He admits him to Hell. And whoever grants anyone the sanctuary of Allah has violated something of the sanctuary of Allah without right; upon him is the curse of Allah, or he said: the protection of Allah, mighty and majestic, is quit of him."
"22","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: al-Masudi narrated to us, he said: Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas narrated to me, from a man, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given seventy thousand who enter Paradise without reckoning, their faces like the moon on the night of fullness, their hearts upon the heart of one man. So I asked increase of my Lord, mighty and majestic, and He increased me with each one seventy thousand. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: So I judged that that reaches the people of the villages and strikes the edges of the deserts."
"23","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Ziyad al-Jassas, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard Abu Bakr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does evil is recompensed for it in this world."
"24","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, he said: Ibn Shihab said: A trustworthy man of the Ansar informed me that he heard Uthman ibn Affan narrate that men of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, grieved for him until some of them almost fell into delusion. Uthman said: So I was among them, and he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Abu al-Yaman from Shuayb."
"25","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Salih, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that Fatima daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, after the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to divide for her her inheritance from what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left of what Allah granted him. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said to her: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not inherited; what we leave is charity. So Fatima, peace be upon her, became angry and forsook Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and remained forsaking him until she died. He said: And she lived after the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) six months. He said: And Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her, used to ask Abu Bakr for her share of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left of Khaybar and Fadak and his charity in Medina, and Abu Bakr refused her that and said: I am not leaving anything the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do except that I do it, and I fear, if I leave anything of his affair, that I will deviate. As for his charity in Medina, Umar gave it to Ali and Abbas, and Ali overcame him for it. As for Khaybar and Fadak, Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, kept them and said: They are the charity of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they were for his needs that befell him and his calamities, and their affair is to whoever holds authority. He said: So they remain so today."
"26","Hasan ibn Musa and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that she quoted this verse while Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, was judging: And a white one through whose face the clouds are asked for rain, a spring for the orphans, a protection for the widows. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: That, by Allah, is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"27","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, he said: My father informed me that the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not know where to bury the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No prophet is buried except where he dies. So they moved his bedding and dug for him beneath his bedding."
"28","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Teach me a supplication to supplicate with in my prayer. He said: Say: O Allah, I have wronged myself with much wrongdoing, and none forgives sins except You, so forgive me with forgiveness from You and have mercy on me; You are the Forgiving, the Merciful."
"29","Hammad ibn Usama narrated to us, he said: Ismail informed us, from Qays, he said: Abu Bakr stood and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, you recite this verse: O you who believe, upon you are yourselves, until he reached the end of the verse. Verily, when people see the wrongdoer and do not seize his hands, Allah will soon envelop them in His punishment. Verily, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Verily, people, and once he said again: And we heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"30","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: O people, you recite this verse: O you who believe, upon you are yourselves; he who strays will not harm you if you are guided, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If people see the wrongdoer and do not seize his hands, Allah will soon envelop them in His punishment."
"31","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hammam informed us, from Farqad al-Sabakhi, and Affan, they said: Murra al-Tayyib narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No one evil in mastery shall enter Paradise."
"32","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sadaqa ibn Musa informed us, from Farqad al-Sabakhi, from Murra al-Tayyib, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No deceitful person shall enter Paradise, nor miser, nor one who reminds of favors, nor one evil in mastery; and the first to enter Paradise is the slave when he obeys Allah and obeys his master."
"33","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from al-Mughira ibn Subay, from Amr ibn Hurayth, that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, recovered from an illness of his and went out to the people and excused himself with something and said: We intended nothing but good. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us that the Dajjal will emerge from a land in the east called Khurasan, followed by peoples whose faces are like hammered shields."
"34","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, he said: I heard Sulaym ibn Amir, a man of Hims, and he had met the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and once he said: He said: I heard Awsat al-Bajali, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard him address the people, and once he said: when he was appointed caliph, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood last year in this place of mine, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, wept and said: I ask Allah for pardon and well-being, for people were not given after certainty anything better than well-being. Hold to truthfulness, for it is in Paradise, and beware of lying, for it is with wickedness, and both are in the Fire. Do not sever ties, do not hate one another, do not envy one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be brothers as Allah, mighty and majestic, commanded you."
"35","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Ayyash, narrated to us, from Asim, from Zir, from Abdullah, that Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, gave him glad tidings that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes to read the Quran fresh as it was revealed, let him read it upon the reading of Ibn Umm Abd."
"36","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Bakr and Yazid ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it; he said: fresh, or moist."
"37","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad and Said ibn Salama ibn Abi al-Husam narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Abu al-Huwayrith, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, that Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I wished I had asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what saves us from what Satan casts into ourselves. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I asked him about that, and he said: What saves you from that is that you say what I commanded my uncle to say."
"38","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed the people and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, people were not given in this world better than certainty and well-being, so ask them of Allah, mighty and majestic."
"39","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: And Husayn ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Ikrima, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When they wanted to dig for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah used to dig as the people of Mecca dig, and Abu Talha Zayd ibn Sahl used to dig for the people of Medina, and he used to make a lahd. Al-Abbas called two men and said to one of them: Go to Abu Ubayda, and to the other: Go to Abu Talha. O Allah, choose for Your Messenger. The companion of Abu Talha found Abu Talha and came with him, so he made a lahd for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"40","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Umar ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, Uqba ibn al-Harith informed me, he said: I went out with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, from the afternoon prayer, nights after the death of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with Ali, peace be upon him, walking beside him. He passed Hasan ibn Ali playing with boys, and carried him upon his neck, saying: By my father, resemblance of the Prophet, not resemblance of Ali. He said: And Ali was laughing."
"41","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Jabir, from Amir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from Abu Bakr, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Maiz ibn Malik came and confessed before him once, and he turned him away. Then he came and confessed before him a second time, and he turned him away. Then he came and confessed a third time, and he turned him away. I said to him: If you confess a fourth time he will stone you. He said: So he confessed a fourth time, so he detained him, then asked about him, and they said: We know nothing but good. He said: So he ordered him stoned."
"42","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Said ibn Dhi Uswan al-Ansi informed me, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr al-Lakhmi, from Rafi al-Tai, companion of Abu Bakr in the expedition of al-Salasil, he said: And I asked him about what was said of their pledge, and he said, while narrating to him what the Ansar said and what he said to them and what Umar ibn al-Khattab said to the Ansar and what he reminded them of his leading them in prayer by the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his illness; so they pledged allegiance to me for that, and I accepted it from them, fearing there would be a trial followed by apostasy."
"43","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Wahshi ibn Harb ibn Wahshi ibn Harb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Wahshi ibn Harb, that Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, appointed Khalid ibn al-Walid over fighting the people of apostasy, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: An excellent servant of Allah and brother of the clan is Khalid ibn al-Walid, a sword of the swords of Allah which Allah, mighty and majestic, unsheathed against the disbelievers and hypocrites."
"44","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Muawiya, meaning Ibn Salih, narrated to us, from Sulaym ibn Amir al-Kalai, from Awsat ibn Amr, he said: I came to Medina a year after the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found Abu Bakr addressing the people. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us last year, and his voice was choked with tears three times, then said: O people, ask Allah for well-being, for no one was given like certainty after well-being, and nothing is worse than doubt after disbelief. Hold to truthfulness, for it guides to righteousness, and both are in Paradise. Beware of lying, for it guides to wickedness, and both are in the Fire."
"45","Muhammad ibn Muyassar Abu Sad al-Saghani, the blind, narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: When death came to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: What day is this? They said: Monday. He said: If I die tonight, do not wait with me till morning, for the most beloved days and nights to me are the nearest to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"46","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, Amr ibn Murra narrated to us, from Abu Ubayda, he said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, stood a year after the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in my place last year and said: Ask Allah for well-being, for no servant was given anything better than well-being. Hold to truthfulness and righteousness, for both are in Paradise. Beware of lying and wickedness, for both are in the Fire."
"47","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughira, he said: I heard Ali ibn Rabia, of Banu Asad, narrate from Asma, or Ibn Asma, of Banu Fazara, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Whenever I heard anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah benefited me with whatever He willed to benefit me of it. Abu Bakr narrated to me, and Abu Bakr spoke the truth; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who commits a sin, then performs ablution and prays two rakas, then seeks forgiveness from Allah Almighty for that sin, except that He forgives him. And he recited these two verses: And whoever does evil or wrongs himself, then seeks forgiveness from Allah, will find Allah Forgiving, Merciful; and: And those who, when they commit indecency or wrong themselves, the verse."
"48","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: I heard Uthman, of the family of Abu Uqayl al-Thaqafi, except that he said: Shuba said: And he recited one of these two verses: Whoever does evil is recompensed for it; and: And those who, when they commit indecency."
"49","Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatada narrate from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman that Umar said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us last year and said: Verily, nothing better than well-being after certainty was divided among people. Verily, truthfulness and righteousness are in Paradise. Verily, lying and wickedness are in the Fire."
"50","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq say: I heard al-Bara say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from Mecca to Medina, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thirsted, and they passed a shepherd of sheep. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, said: So I took a cup and milked in it for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a measure of milk, and brought it to him, and he drank until I was satisfied."
"51","Bahz narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, Yala ibn Ata narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Asim say: I heard Abu Hurayra say: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something to say when I rise in the morning and when I enter the evening and when I take my bed. He said: Say: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, or he said: O Allah, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Lord of everything and its Sovereign, I bear witness that there is no god but You; I seek refuge in You from the evil of myself and the evil of Satan and his association."
"52","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, he said: I heard Amr ibn Asim ibn Abdullah, and he mentioned its meaning."
"53","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Ismail, he said: I heard Qays ibn Abi Hazim narrate from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, that he addressed and said: O people, you recite this verse and place it upon other than what Allah placed it: O you who believe, upon you are yourselves; he who strays will not harm you if you are guided. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If people see evil among them and do not denounce it, Allah will soon envelop them in His punishment."
"54","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Tawba al-Anbari, he said: I heard Abu Sawwar the judge say, from Abu Barza al-Aslami, he said: A man spoke harshly to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: Abu Barza said: Shall I strike his neck? He said: So he rebuked him and said: It belongs to no one after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"55","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she informed him that Fatima daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, asking her inheritance from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of what Allah granted him in Medina and Fadak and what remained of the fifth of Khaybar. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not inherited; what we leave is charity; the family of Muhammad only eats from this wealth. By Allah, I will not change anything of the charity of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the state it was upon in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I will act therein as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) acted. So Abu Bakr refused to give Fatima anything of it, and Fatima found resentment against Abu Bakr in that. Abu Bakr said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the kinship of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is more beloved to me to join than my own kinship. As for what arose between me and you of these properties, I did not spare therein from the truth, and I did not leave any matter I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do therein except that I did it."
"56","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Zara narrated to us, from Ali ibn Rabia, from Asma ibn al-Hakam al-Fazari, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah ennoble his face, say: Whenever I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah benefited me with it with whatever He willed to benefit me of it, and when another narrated to me I made him swear, and if he swore to me I believed him. Abu Bakr narrated to me, and Abu Bakr spoke the truth; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no believing servant who commits a sin and then performs ablution and performs purification well, then prays two rakas and seeks forgiveness from Allah Almighty, except that Allah forgives him. Then he recited: And those who, when they commit indecency or wrong themselves."
"57","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, sent to me at the killing of the people of Yamama. Abu Bakr said: O Zayd ibn Thabit, you are a young, intelligent youth whom we do not suspect; you used to write revelation for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so pursue the Quran and collect it."
"58","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that Fatima and al-Abbas came to Abu Bakr seeking their inheritance from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then seeking his land of Fadak and his share of Khaybar. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them, said to them: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: We are not inherited; what we leave is charity, and the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only eats from this wealth. By Allah, I will not abandon any matter I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do therein except that I do it."
"59","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Nafi, meaning Ibn Umar, narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, he said: It was said to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him: O caliph of Allah. He said: I am the caliph of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I am content with it, and I am content with it, and I am content."
"60","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salama, that Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her, said to Abu Bakr: Who inherits you when you die? He said: My children and my family. She said: Then why do we not inherit the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Prophet is not inherited, but I support whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to support, and I spend upon whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to spend."
"61","Affan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir, that he narrated to them, from Abu Barza al-Aslami, that he said: We were with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, in his work, and he became angry at a man of the Muslims, and his anger against him intensified greatly. When I saw that I said: O caliph of the Messenger of Allah, shall I strike his neck? When I mentioned killing, he turned from that talk entirely to other talk of the sort. When we dispersed, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, sent to me after that and said: O Abu Barza, what did you say? He said: And I had forgotten what I said. I said: Remind me of it. He said: Do you not remember what you said? He said: I said: No, by Allah. He said: Did you see when I became angry at the man and you said: Shall I strike his neck, O caliph of the Messenger of Allah; do you not remember that, and would you have done it? He said: I said: Yes, by Allah, and now if you command me I will do it. He said: Woe to you, or: Alas for you; that, by Allah, belongs to no one after Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"62","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Atiq narrated to us, from his father, that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The tooth-stick purifies the mouth and pleases the Lord."
"63","Affan narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, he said: I heard Amr ibn Asim ibn Abdullah, he said: I heard Abu Hurayra say: Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, say for me something to say when I rise in the morning and when I enter the evening. He said: Say: O Allah, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Lord of everything and its Sovereign, I bear witness that there is no god but You; I seek refuge in You from the evil of myself and from the evil of Satan and his association. And he commanded him to say it when he rises in the morning and when he enters the evening and when he takes his bed."
"64","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Nafi ibn Umar al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulayka, he said: It was said to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him: O caliph of Allah. He said: Rather the caliph of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I am content with it."
"65","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Muammal narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, he said: The bridle would sometimes fall from the hand of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him; he said: So he would strike the foreleg of his camel and make it kneel and take it. He said: They said to him: Why did you not command us to hand it to you? He said: My beloved, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), commanded me not to ask people for anything."
"66","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu Ubayda, from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, stood a year after the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us last year and said: The son of Adam was not given anything better than well-being, so ask Allah for well-being. Hold to truthfulness and righteousness, for both are in Paradise. Beware of lying and wickedness, for both are in the Fire."
"67","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Masud, from Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah; when they say it, they protect from me their blood and wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah Almighty. He said: When the apostasy occurred, Umar said to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them: Will you fight them though you heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say such-and-such? Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: By Allah, I will not separate between prayer and alms-tax, and I will fight whoever separates between them. He said: So we fought with him, and we judged that guidance."
"68","Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Ismail informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Zuhayr, he said: I was informed that Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, how is soundness after this verse: It is not by your wishes nor the wishes of the People of the Book; whoever does evil is recompensed for it; for every evil we did we are recompensed? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah forgive you, O Abu Bakr; do you not fall ill, do you not tire, do you not grieve, does hardship not befall you? He said: Yes. He said: So it is what you are recompensed with."
"69","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Zuhayr, I think he said: Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, how is soundness after this verse? He said: May Allah have mercy on you, O Abu Bakr; do you not fall ill, do you not grieve, does hardship not befall you? He said: Yes. He said: Then that is with that. Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us."
"70","Ismail narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Thaqafi, he said: Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, how is soundness after this verse: Whoever does evil is recompensed for it; and he mentioned the hadith."
"71","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Zuhayr al-Thaqafi, he said: When: It is not by your wishes nor the wishes of the People of the Book; whoever does evil is recompensed for it, was revealed, he said: Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, we shall indeed be recompensed for every evil we do. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on you, O Abu Bakr; do you not tire, do you not grieve, does hardship not befall you? This is what you are recompensed with."
"72","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: I took this book from Thumama ibn Abdullah ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, that Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote to them: These are the obligations of charity which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) obligated upon the Muslims, which Allah, mighty and majestic, thereby commanded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Whoever of the Muslims is asked for it in its proper manner, let him give it, and whoever is asked above that, let him not give it. For fewer than twenty-five camels, for every five camels a sheep. When they reach twenty-five, therein is a she-camel in its second year up to thirty-five; if there is no she-camel in its second year, then a male camel in its third year. When they reach thirty-six, therein is a she-camel in its third year up to forty-five. When they reach forty-six, therein is a she-camel in its fourth year, fit for mating, up to sixty. When they reach sixty-one, therein is a she-camel in its fifth year up to seventy-five. When they reach seventy-six, therein are two she-camels in their third year up to ninety. When they reach ninety-one, therein are two she-camels in their fourth year, fit for mating, up to one hundred twenty. If they exceed one hundred twenty, then for every forty a she-camel in its third year, and for every fifty a she-camel in its fourth year. When the ages of camels differ in the obligations of charities, whoever owes a she-camel in its fifth year and does not have it but has one in its fourth year, it is accepted from him, and he gives with it two sheep if they are easy for him, or twenty dirhams. Whoever owes a she-camel in its fourth year and has only one in its fifth year, it is accepted from him, and the collector gives him twenty dirhams or two sheep. Whoever owes a she-camel in its fourth year and does not have it but has a she-camel in its third year, it is accepted from him, and he gives with it two sheep if they are easy for him, or twenty dirhams. Whoever owes a she-camel in its third year and has only one in its fourth year, it is accepted from him, and the collector gives him twenty dirhams or two sheep. Whoever owes a she-camel in its third year and does not have a she-camel in its third year but has a she-camel in its second year, it is accepted from him, and he gives with it two sheep if they are easy for him, or twenty dirhams. Whoever owes a she-camel in its second year and has only a male camel in its third year, it is accepted from him, and nothing is with it. Whoever has only four camels has nothing therein unless its owner wishes. For the charity of sheep in their pastured ones, when they are forty, therein is a sheep up to one hundred twenty; if they increase, therein are two sheep up to two hundred; if one increases, therein are three sheep up to three hundred; if they increase, then for every hundred a sheep. No decrepit animal is taken in charity, nor one with defect, nor a he-goat, unless the collector wishes. What is scattered is not joined, nor what is joined is separated, out of fear of charity. Whatever belongs to two partners, they settle between them equally. When a man's pastured animals are one short of forty sheep, there is nothing therein unless its owner wishes. For silver, a quarter of a tenth; if the wealth is only one hundred ninety dirhams, there is nothing therein unless its owner wishes."
"73","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: The people of Mecca say: Ibn Jurayj took the prayer from Ata, and Ata took it from Ibn al-Zubayr, and Ibn al-Zubayr took it from Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr took it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I never saw anyone with better prayer than Ibn Jurayj."
"74","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, he said: Hafsa daughter of Umar became widowed from Khunays, or Hudhayfa ibn Hudhafa, Abd al-Razzaq doubted, and he was of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who witnessed Badr, and died in Medina. He said: So I met Uthman ibn Affan and offered him Hafsa, and said: If you wish, I will marry you to Hafsa. He said: I will consider that. I waited nights, then he met me and said: I do not wish to marry these days of mine. Umar said: So I met Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: If you wish, I will marry you to Hafsa daughter of Umar, and he did not return anything to me, and I was angrier with him than with Uthman. I waited nights, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed her to me, and I married her to him. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, met me and said: Perhaps you found against me when you offered me Hafsa and I did not return anything to you. He said: I said: Yes. He said: Nothing prevented me from returning anything to you when you offered her to me except that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention her, and I would not disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); had he left her, I would have married her."
"75","Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Mughira ibn Muslim Abu Salama, from Farqad al-Sabakhi, from Murra al-Tayyib, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one evil in mastery shall enter Paradise. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not inform us that this nation has the most slaves and orphans of the nations? He said: Yes, so honor them as you honor your children, and feed them of what you eat. They said: Then what benefits us in this world, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A sound horse you tie to fight upon in the path of Allah, and a slave who suffices you; when he prays, he is your brother."
"76","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Ibn al-Sabbaq informed me, he said: Zayd ibn Thabit informed me that Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, sent to him at the killing of the people of Yamama, and Umar was with him. Abu Bakr said: Umar came to me and said: Killing has fallen heavily upon the reciters of the Quran of the Muslims of the people of Yamama, and I fear killing will fall heavily upon the reciters in the battlefields, and much Quran will go unpreserved. I judge that you command the collection of the Quran. I said to Umar: How do I do something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do? He said: By Allah it is good. He kept returning to me therein until Allah expanded my breast thereby, and I judged therein what Umar judged. Zayd said, with Umar sitting with him not speaking: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: You are a young, intelligent youth whom we do not suspect, and you used to write revelation for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so collect it. Zayd said: By Allah, had they charged me with moving a mountain of the mountains, it would not have been heavier upon me than what they commanded me of collecting the Quran. I said: How do you do something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do?"
"77","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Umayr, freedman of al-Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken and Abu Bakr was made caliph, al-Abbas disputed with Ali over things the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left and did not move, I will not move. When Umar was made caliph, they disputed to him, and he said: Something Abu Bakr did not move, I will not move. He said: When Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, was made caliph, they disputed to him. He said: So Uthman fell silent and bowed his head. Ibn Abbas said: So I feared he would take it, and I struck with my hand between the shoulders of al-Abbas and said: Father, I adjure you except that you surrender it to Ali. He said: So he surrendered it to him."
"78","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, he said: A shaykh of Quraysh of Banu Taym narrated to me, he said: So-and-so and so-and-so narrated to me, and he said: He counted six or seven, all of Quraysh, among them Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: While we were sitting with Umar, Ali and al-Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, entered with raised voices. Umar said: Hush, O Abbas, I know what you say: you say: son of my brother, and I have half the wealth; and I know what you say, O Ali: you say: his daughter is under me, and she has half the wealth. This is what was in the hands of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we saw how he acted therein. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, held it after him and acted therein with the action of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then I held it after Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and I swear by Allah I will strive to act therein with the action of the Messenger of Allah and the action of Abu Bakr. Then he said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, and he swore that he is truthful, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Prophet is not inherited, and his inheritance is only for the poor and needy of the Muslims. And Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, and he swore by Allah that he is truthful, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No prophet dies until some of his nation leads him in prayer. This is what was in the hands of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we saw how he acted therein. If you wish, I will give it to you to act therein with the action of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the action of Abu Bakr until I hand it to you. He said: So they withdrew, then came, and al-Abbas said: Hand it to Ali, for I have made my soul content with it for him."
"79","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, that Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her, came to Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, seeking her inheritance from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: We heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am not inherited."
"80","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Isa, meaning Ibn al-Musayyab, narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: I was sitting with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, caliph of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a month after the death of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned a story. The people were called: Prayer is assembling, and it was the first prayer among the Muslims in which: Prayer is assembling, was called. The people gathered, and he ascended the minbar, a thing made for him upon which he used to address, and it was the first address he addressed in Islam. He said: So he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, I wished another than me had sufficed me this, and if you take me with the practice of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I cannot bear it; he was protected from Satan, and revelation used to descend upon him from heaven."
"81","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, he said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to say when I rise in the morning and when I enter the evening and when I take my bed at night: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, You are Lord of everything and its Sovereign, I bear witness that there is no god but You alone, no partner for You, and that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger. I seek refuge in You from the evil of myself and the evil of Satan and his association, and that I commit evil against myself or bring it upon a Muslim. End of the musnad of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him."
